WEBVTT

00:07.750 --> 00:11.040
We are succeeding in minimizing
the attacks against our transport trains.

00:11.670 --> 00:13.710
And we are dominating in the marketplace.

00:13.710 --> 00:16.250
The Major Corporate Alliance lacks
the Wisdom of the Shadows.

00:16.250 --> 00:19.580
So their attempts to supply paper money and
create credit will be more than they can handle.

00:19.580 --> 00:21.420
If these circumstances continue,

00:21.420 --> 00:24.630
I believe they will be crushed under
the weight of their own ambition.

00:24.830 --> 00:26.250
Just as we predicted.

00:26.250 --> 00:28.500
But remember, as I'm sure you know...

00:29.130 --> 00:33.580
We will not take any actions that would imply
Mitsugoshi has a connection to Shadow Garden.

00:34.000 --> 00:38.130
Of course, that will force us to
rely on passive measures...

00:38.460 --> 00:41.000
It only takes a moment for trust to be destroyed.

00:41.000 --> 00:44.380
We must devote the utmost care
to maintaining that trust.

00:44.630 --> 00:46.290
Surely he taught you that, as well.

00:46.290 --> 00:47.290
Indeed.

00:47.290 --> 00:50.080
For now, we must refrain from any brash behavior.

00:52.710 --> 00:54.130
I beg your pardon.

00:54.130 --> 00:55.500
But we have guests.

00:55.500 --> 00:59.500
Unlike Garter Kikuchi, it seems
this man has little patience.

00:59.500 --> 01:00.960
He's young.

01:01.170 --> 01:04.580
He can't suppress his warrior-
or rather, his therianthrope nature.

01:04.920 --> 01:06.210
In any case, Nu.

01:06.210 --> 01:08.170
I know it's late, but treat our guests with the proper-

01:08.170 --> 01:09.380
Lady Alpha...

01:10.420 --> 01:12.830
Please allow me to handle this.

01:12.830 --> 01:13.830
What?

01:13.830 --> 01:14.830
What?

01:18.750 --> 01:20.130
In any case, Nu...

01:20.130 --> 01:22.170
I know it's late, but treat our guests with the proper-

01:22.170 --> 01:23.380
Lady Alpha...

01:23.790 --> 01:25.880
Please allow me to handle this.

01:27.920 --> 01:29.130
You?

01:29.750 --> 01:30.750
Yes, Lady Alpha.

01:30.750 --> 01:32.580
I will teach our visitors a lesson.

01:33.080 --> 01:34.290
Really...

01:34.630 --> 01:36.750
You two, go with her.

01:41.420 --> 01:43.000
Well, I'm sure it will be fine.

01:43.380 --> 01:45.460
She is seventeen years old, after all.

01:45.630 --> 01:46.830
What?

01:46.830 --> 01:48.040
What?

01:51.130 --> 01:52.330
What?

01:58.750 --> 02:00.830
That is too late

02:00.830 --> 02:03.750
You can't catch up with a move like that anymore
Sonna te ja mou oitsukenai<b></b>

02:03.750 --> 02:05.880
That is to say...

02:08.830 --> 02:15.040
The first move chooses an unknown future
Saisho no itte de erabu michi naru future<b></b>

02:15.040 --> 02:17.380
How it will be
Sono arisama<b></b>

02:17.710 --> 02:18.830
This way

02:18.830 --> 02:25.080
The last move decides the world's answer
Saigo no itte de kimeru sekai no answer<b></b>

02:25.080 --> 02:27.750
A single winner
Hitori no winner<b></b>

02:27.750 --> 02:29.130
It's me

02:29.380 --> 02:31.670
These eyes have seen it
Kono me wa misueta<b></b>

02:33.170 --> 02:38.750
The optimal solution no one has yet been able to discern
Dare mo imada mitoosenu saitekikai o<b></b>

02:40.040 --> 02:43.830
It's all a game to control the board
Subete wa banjou shihai suru game<b></b>

02:43.830 --> 02:46.330
A battle of thought
Shikou no tousou<b></b>

02:46.500 --> 02:48.880
I disguise even my mistakes
Mistake sae mo gisou shite<b></b>

02:48.880 --> 02:51.460
And even checkmate is a preparatory move
Checkmate made fuseki toshite<b></b>

02:51.460 --> 02:53.880
A game to take each other's king
King o ubaiau game<b></b>

02:53.880 --> 02:56.330
Ideology and desire
Shisou to yokubou<b></b>

02:56.630 --> 02:59.000
A bad move to not let one chance get away
One chance minogasanu akushu<b></b>

02:59.000 --> 03:01.670
The last chance will cinch it
Last chance kanarazu shitomeru<b></b>

03:01.920 --> 03:03.920
That is too late

03:03.920 --> 03:06.830
You can't catch up with a move like that anymore
Sonna te ja mou oitsukenai<b></b>

03:06.830 --> 03:09.040
That is to say

03:09.040 --> 03:14.000
Total victory is in my hands
Kanzen shouri wa kono te no naka ni<b></b>

03:19.290 --> 03:22.080
No one can catch up now
Dare nimo mou oitsukenai<b></b>

03:23.080 --> 03:28.000
<b>#05 He Who Pulls the Strings</b>

03:32.250 --> 03:33.920
It was awfully easy to get in.

03:34.250 --> 03:36.880
They're probably using all their security
to guard their transports.

03:37.790 --> 03:41.210
Our target is the manager,
an elf woman known as Luna.

03:41.630 --> 03:43.040
Let's find her office.

03:45.210 --> 03:46.420
Is that...

03:47.170 --> 03:49.380
Thank you for coming to Mitsugoshi.

03:49.380 --> 03:51.880
I am the manager, Luna.

03:51.880 --> 03:54.210
And I am here to welcome you.

03:56.750 --> 03:57.960
What?!

03:59.380 --> 04:02.790
But there's no sign of any bodyguard.

04:02.790 --> 04:04.920
Her confidence is a bluff.

04:05.330 --> 04:09.130
I am the man who earned the title of Leaf One,
strongest of the Clovers.

04:09.130 --> 04:11.960
No one has engaged me in battle
and come out unscathed!

04:13.250 --> 04:16.580
If you don't want to die,
then be a good girl and say goodnight!

04:17.250 --> 04:20.830
That hurts!

04:23.130 --> 04:24.330
Y-you...

04:24.710 --> 04:25.920
Huh?

04:25.920 --> 04:26.960
Ugh!

04:26.960 --> 04:29.830
In these situations, you start with a powerful
frontal attack and then just play it by ear!

04:29.830 --> 04:31.880
Don't you know that?

04:33.250 --> 04:35.460
This is the trouble with entitled customers!

04:37.330 --> 04:39.830
<i>That black artifact...</i>

04:39.830 --> 04:41.040
<i>It can't be!</i>

04:44.540 --> 04:45.750
<i>She's fast!</i>

04:46.040 --> 04:47.040
<i>But...</i>

04:47.040 --> 04:48.000
Take that and that and that and that and that!

04:48.000 --> 04:50.000
<i>That's all she is.
</i>Take that and that and that and that and that!<b></b>

04:50.130 --> 04:52.790
<i>She's fast, but she's a total amateur!
</i>Take that and that and that and that and that!<b></b>

04:52.790 --> 04:54.000
And that!

04:57.170 --> 05:01.380
That footwork, you're a student of the
Western Liechtenroi style of fencing, aren't you?

05:01.380 --> 05:02.380
<i>What?</i>

05:02.380 --> 05:04.630
<i>In just a few seconds, she identified my fighting style?</i>

05:04.630 --> 05:07.290
Now that I know your style, I can easily counter it!

05:07.290 --> 05:08.790
Take that and that and that!

05:08.790 --> 05:12.210
<i>She should be able to predict my every move now,
</i>Take that and that and that and that and that!<b></b>

05:12.210 --> 05:14.290
<i>but her approach is still exactly the same!
</i>Take that and that and that and that and that!<b></b>

05:14.290 --> 05:15.710
<i>She is an amateur!
</i>Take that and that and that and that and that!<b></b>

05:18.790 --> 05:21.750
That hurts!

05:25.790 --> 05:27.830
<i>I was absolutely sure that was a direct hit!</i>

05:27.830 --> 05:30.130
<i>So why? What in blue blazes is going on?!</i>

05:31.460 --> 05:34.790
You are a skilled warrior to land a hit on me!

05:34.790 --> 05:36.000
Very well.

05:36.000 --> 05:39.750
I grant you the honor of facing my full fury for that!

05:43.290 --> 05:44.500
<i>Dammit!</i>

05:44.500 --> 05:46.630
<i>What is with all that excessive magical energy?!</i>

05:46.630 --> 05:48.040
<i>And that battle cry!</i>

05:50.330 --> 05:53.040
Hear what my great lord and master taught me.

05:54.380 --> 05:56.170
Yeah, lemme think...

05:56.170 --> 05:57.830
For you, Gamma...

05:58.380 --> 06:01.580
Your stats are ridiculously high, so...

06:01.580 --> 06:03.250
To start with...

06:03.830 --> 06:06.880
"Jam a lot of magical energy into it and hack away!"

06:09.460 --> 06:12.830
"And when you slash,
make sure to look intimidating!"

06:12.830 --> 06:14.040
Take that and-

06:23.750 --> 06:24.960
Huh?

06:27.880 --> 06:29.420
Well played, my good sir.

06:29.420 --> 06:31.960
Acting as though you were only evading my attack

06:31.960 --> 06:34.920
while using the lay of the land to set a clever trap.

06:36.170 --> 06:39.080
I'd expect nothing less of a grand master
of the Liechtenroi style.

06:39.580 --> 06:41.000
Your nose is bleeding.

06:41.880 --> 06:45.040
Uh, anyway, I don't want anything more
to do with this woman-

06:45.040 --> 06:46.250
I mean!

06:46.250 --> 06:50.040
Apparently, this woman is too much for me to handle.

06:50.710 --> 06:53.630
Men! It's time you quit messing around!
We need to beat a tactical-

06:53.630 --> 06:55.250
As for your missing children...

06:56.420 --> 06:58.290
We have been looking after them for you.

07:00.920 --> 07:02.630
Be careful, you two!

07:03.670 --> 07:06.750
That man has mastered the Liechtenroi technique.

07:06.750 --> 07:09.420
He's most likely one of the greatest
fencers in the entire world!

07:09.710 --> 07:11.380
That is impressive.

07:12.420 --> 07:15.000
No, I'm not! I'm just...

07:16.460 --> 07:19.880
But I have seen the secret behind
your eminent power.

07:19.880 --> 07:22.250
From now on, I will show you my full strength!

07:23.580 --> 07:25.210
<i>Please make it stop...</i>

07:26.630 --> 07:27.630
Damn it all!

07:27.630 --> 07:29.290
You won't get away from me!

07:29.290 --> 07:30.790
Taaake tha-

07:32.790 --> 07:34.000
Hup!

08:01.040 --> 08:02.880
That was my secret technique:

08:03.880 --> 08:05.920
the Self Sacrifice Spinning Wheel.

08:07.540 --> 08:09.210
Your nose is bleeding.

08:11.080 --> 08:13.420
The Clovers haven't returned, you say?

08:13.420 --> 08:21.830
<b>Late Night Explosion at Mitsugoshi.</b>

08:13.420 --> 08:21.830
<b>Was It an Accident?</b>

08:13.880 --> 08:15.420
Y-yes, sir.

08:15.420 --> 08:18.000
Neither have the reinforcements we sent.

08:18.000 --> 08:21.130
And we even lost contact with the lookout team.

08:22.330 --> 08:27.290
Mr. Gettan, there are members of the MCA
that have ties with Mitsugoshi.

08:27.290 --> 08:28.540
I'm afraid this failure-

08:28.540 --> 08:32.130
I mean, this incident will get them talking again.

08:32.130 --> 08:33.330
Then shut them up.

08:35.420 --> 08:36.750
Y-yes, sir.

08:42.330 --> 08:44.830
I should have known that naming them Clovers

08:44.830 --> 08:48.170
wouldn't make those sorry excuses for bandits
equal to the Knights.

08:48.790 --> 08:51.500
I would have liked to use some of the Children,

08:51.500 --> 08:53.580
but the Cult is running low on resources, as well.

08:54.000 --> 08:56.420
First Zenon, then that old fossil.

08:56.420 --> 08:59.380
They're both dead, but they're still getting in my way.

08:59.380 --> 09:03.960
But that is exactly why this is the perfect opportunity
for me to demonstrate my power.

09:04.580 --> 09:07.460
The Major Corporate Alliance is
nothing more than a disposable pawn.

09:07.790 --> 09:11.420
I only need them to stay afloat long enough
for me to complete my preparations.

09:12.710 --> 09:14.830
Just a little while longer.

09:16.130 --> 09:17.670
Soon...

09:21.130 --> 09:22.790
I will have power.

09:22.790 --> 09:26.290
Power that no one will be able to take from me!

09:58.960 --> 10:00.170
Well?

10:00.170 --> 10:01.420
I think you did well.

10:01.710 --> 10:03.710
And I think you'll probably just keep getting better.

10:05.130 --> 10:06.330
Really?

10:06.960 --> 10:09.500
<i>Was it a change of mindset?</i>

10:09.500 --> 10:12.040
<i>Or did she figure something out?</i>

10:12.630 --> 10:15.880
<i>When a character suddenly gets a lot better,
it's usually one of those things.</i>

10:16.670 --> 10:18.210
But it's not enough.

10:18.960 --> 10:20.830
I need more power.

10:21.170 --> 10:22.170
Cool...

10:23.710 --> 10:25.380
Ask me why.

10:25.920 --> 10:27.130
Why?

10:27.540 --> 10:31.040
Because all I could do was watch.

10:31.920 --> 10:34.210
Now Rose has gone off alone.

10:35.080 --> 10:37.290
Oriana has lost its king.

10:37.290 --> 10:40.670
It's a real mess right now, and she's...

10:42.250 --> 10:44.710
My friend is suffering, and I...

10:46.170 --> 10:48.880
I need more power,

10:48.880 --> 10:51.130
and there are a lot of other things
that I'm lacking, too.

10:51.540 --> 10:55.080
While we lead our everyday lives,
the world keeps moving forward in secret.

11:01.170 --> 11:04.630
If I don't move with it, I'll be left behind.

11:06.750 --> 11:09.170
I don't want to be an outsider anymore.

11:10.040 --> 11:11.250
Uh-huh...

11:13.580 --> 11:14.790
It's strange.

11:15.580 --> 11:20.380
Since I started actively choosing to move forward,
time has started to move faster.

11:20.880 --> 11:22.290
That's just how it is.

11:23.420 --> 11:25.460
You're so carefree.
That must be nice.

11:30.080 --> 11:33.500
I sincerely hope you can be that
carefree your whole life.

12:00.790 --> 12:04.420
Extra large char siu, with extra veggies,
no back fat or garlic.

12:04.420 --> 12:05.630
Coming up.

12:10.040 --> 12:12.130
Production is complete.

12:16.290 --> 12:17.500
Then it's time.

12:22.460 --> 12:23.460
Here you go, enjoy.

12:24.250 --> 12:26.630
The domain formerly ruled by Viscount Grease...

12:26.630 --> 12:29.380
It is currently run by a disinterested local magistrate,

12:29.380 --> 12:31.500
and law enforcement is less than thorough.

12:32.210 --> 12:35.040
Naturally, they wouldn't bother
sparing any personnel

12:35.040 --> 12:37.080
to inspect the abandoned mine
at the edge of the domain.

12:37.630 --> 12:40.540
I am truly happy that this place has been
brought to my attention.

12:41.330 --> 12:43.540
We produce our counterfeit bills here,

12:43.540 --> 12:45.750
and transport them temporarily to the Lawless City.

12:45.750 --> 12:48.330
Then, we disguise our distribution channels

12:48.330 --> 12:50.500
and introduce them to the Royal Capital of Midgar.

12:52.380 --> 12:54.250
What do you think, Mr. Smith?

12:54.960 --> 12:57.750
For all the time we devoted to
creating the printing plates,

12:57.750 --> 12:59.880
I believe the finished product is quite good, don't you?

13:01.130 --> 13:05.710
Of the two, can you tell which is the authentic bill?

13:10.460 --> 13:11.920
The answer goes without saying.

13:14.330 --> 13:17.500
On comparison, one of them uses paper
of slightly coarser quality.

13:18.080 --> 13:20.580
There are differences in the bleed of the ink.

13:20.580 --> 13:23.290
And surely I don't need to describe
the distortions in the print?

13:23.290 --> 13:24.750
It's true!

13:24.750 --> 13:26.830
But we double- and triple-checked!

13:27.290 --> 13:28.710
I don't need to bullsh-

13:29.000 --> 13:30.880
...point out any more than that, do I?

13:32.330 --> 13:33.630
You do not.

13:33.630 --> 13:35.710
Obviously the bill of lesser quality...

13:35.710 --> 13:37.210
...is the real one.
...is the fake.<b></b>

13:37.420 --> 13:38.420
What?

13:38.420 --> 13:39.420
What?

13:44.880 --> 13:46.670
It appears that you perfected it
to such a high degree

13:46.670 --> 13:48.960
that you have surpassed the authentic article.

13:49.460 --> 13:51.210
I had not foreseen that possibility.

13:52.040 --> 13:53.920
Shall we start over and make new ones?

13:54.170 --> 13:55.580
That won't be necessary.

13:55.960 --> 13:58.540
I doubt anyone other than myself will
be able to tell the difference.

13:59.000 --> 14:01.040
I am no match for your intellect, Mr. Smith.

14:01.670 --> 14:04.170
I was thinking we would begin
distribution right away.

14:04.170 --> 14:05.460
Does that suit you?

14:05.460 --> 14:06.460
Yes.

14:07.580 --> 14:11.130
Once there are more bills in circulation,
the authorities will look for the source.

14:11.420 --> 14:15.290
I am counting on you, Mr. Smith,
to handle that situation as planned.

14:16.960 --> 14:22.500
But that man Gettan is mine.

14:22.960 --> 14:24.460
Revenge?

14:26.290 --> 14:29.330
Gettan took everything from me.

14:31.000 --> 14:35.250
My mother, my friends, my entire village...

14:36.380 --> 14:37.920
Now it's my turn.

14:38.500 --> 14:41.830
I will take everything from him.

14:42.830 --> 14:44.330
I will kill him,

14:44.330 --> 14:46.710
but not until after I have taken it all.

14:51.580 --> 14:53.000
Have it your way.

14:53.420 --> 14:57.290
But take care that you don't turn down the wrong path.

15:02.960 --> 15:04.170
Counterfeit bills?

15:04.170 --> 15:07.630
Yes, of the Major Corporate Alliance's currency.

15:07.630 --> 15:10.380
We found them in several of our stores
throughout the Royal Capital.

15:10.920 --> 15:15.380
Then our decision to accept our
competitor's bills has borne fruit.

15:15.920 --> 15:20.380
Although originally that was so we could
take credit away from their currency.

15:21.380 --> 15:22.920
How much is in circulation?

15:22.920 --> 15:24.290
Not much yet.

15:24.830 --> 15:28.330
The customers who paid with them are unaware
that the bills were counterfeit,

15:28.330 --> 15:30.330
so we haven't determined
where they snuck in from.

15:30.960 --> 15:33.380
Does the Major Corporate Alliance know about this?

15:33.380 --> 15:35.290
They don't seem to have realized yet.

15:35.670 --> 15:38.750
They're working to issue more bills,
without a care in the world.

15:39.330 --> 15:41.080
See to it that they do realize.

15:41.080 --> 15:45.460
If the citizens find out that their money is counterfeit,
we'll have a crisis on our hands.

15:45.460 --> 15:49.380
If anything happens to inspire doubt
in the value of paper money,

15:49.380 --> 15:51.000
it will hurt our business, as well.

15:51.750 --> 15:52.960
No, impossible.

15:53.670 --> 15:55.330
Was that their plan all along?

15:56.210 --> 15:58.290
To instigate a credit collapse?

15:59.000 --> 16:01.380
But they would bring about their own downfall.

16:01.670 --> 16:02.880
Lady Alpha?

16:03.750 --> 16:05.080
It's nothing.

16:05.080 --> 16:07.380
Find out where the counterfeit bills are coming from.

16:07.380 --> 16:08.670
That's our top priority.

16:09.130 --> 16:10.330
Yes, Lady Alpha.

16:11.830 --> 16:14.670
If this turns out to be more than a minor cash grab...

16:15.290 --> 16:16.790
Then who could be behind it?

16:17.290 --> 16:18.710
And why?

16:19.630 --> 16:21.290
A counterfeit bill, you say?

16:21.290 --> 16:22.290
Yes, sir.

16:22.290 --> 16:25.500
A cashier at one of our corporate stores
found it just a little while ago.

16:31.790 --> 16:33.000
Which is it?

16:33.000 --> 16:34.000
Sir?

16:34.000 --> 16:36.460
Oh, yes, of course, it was...

16:37.170 --> 16:39.540
The poorly made one...

16:39.540 --> 16:41.170
I think, maybe?

16:44.420 --> 16:45.670
No matter.

16:45.670 --> 16:47.000
Find out where it came from.

16:47.000 --> 16:49.630
Yes, sir.
Right away, sir!

16:54.000 --> 16:56.960
The number of banknotes we have in circulation

16:56.960 --> 17:00.920
already exceeds the total value of the MCA
assets that give them their credit.

17:01.750 --> 17:05.250
The same should be true for Mitsugoshi.

17:05.580 --> 17:08.130
The only thing that can guarantee the
value of paper money anymore

17:08.130 --> 17:12.420
is the vague concept of the "credit"
given to it by the unenlightened masses.

17:13.210 --> 17:14.630
A counterfeit bill...

17:15.000 --> 17:16.960
A piece of paper like the banknotes,

17:16.960 --> 17:19.500
but without the guaranteed value
promised to the real ones,

17:19.500 --> 17:21.580
it is a genuine, bona fide, worthless scrap of paper.

17:22.080 --> 17:24.130
If the world were to learn of their existence,

17:24.130 --> 17:27.330
every citizen would simultaneously
begin to harbor doubts.

17:27.830 --> 17:30.830
They will fear that even the
real bills in their own wallets

17:30.830 --> 17:33.500
may be nothing more than paper.

17:34.170 --> 17:37.630
Those offhand feelings, that vague ideation...

17:37.630 --> 17:40.170
that is what will cause the collapse of the
credit given to paper money.

17:40.920 --> 17:46.290
That is why we had been preparing to begin
circulating our own counterfeit paper bills.

17:47.040 --> 17:49.880
By intentionally bringing about the downfall of credit,

17:49.880 --> 17:54.460
we would bankrupt the Major Corporate Alliance,
and the abominable Mitsugoshi company with it.

17:54.710 --> 17:57.380
That was the mission given to me by the Cult.

17:57.830 --> 18:01.170
But the plan wasn't supposed to go into effect

18:01.170 --> 18:04.460
until after we had recovered all the Cult assets
that were hidden within the MCA.

18:05.000 --> 18:09.540
Those assets are mixed up in those of our more
public businesses and organizations.

18:10.170 --> 18:12.790
It should take time and effort to retrieve them.

18:13.330 --> 18:16.130
Did they not understand that
when they enacted this plan?

18:16.960 --> 18:21.000
If we sit back and watch as the
counterfeit bills go into circulation,

18:21.000 --> 18:25.290
the Cult could end up losing
enormous amounts of money.

18:26.080 --> 18:27.670
What is this?

18:27.670 --> 18:29.170
What is happening?

18:41.960 --> 18:43.420
Confirming target.

18:44.000 --> 18:46.880
We know that this train is carrying
cargo from the Lawless City.

18:46.880 --> 18:50.250
And that cargo includes the counterfeit bills
mingled with other stolen goods.

18:50.540 --> 18:52.960
We will let other teams search for the counterfeiters

18:52.960 --> 18:55.170
while we move to recover the bills in question.

18:55.750 --> 18:58.170
Number 666, you do not make any decisions.

18:58.790 --> 19:00.960
I am the leader, and you will follow my orders.

19:01.670 --> 19:03.040
I understand that.

19:03.750 --> 19:06.170
No, you don't.
That's why I'm reminding you.

19:06.170 --> 19:08.460
The last mission, the one before that...

19:08.460 --> 19:10.710
What are you so panicked about?

19:11.040 --> 19:13.210
I am not panicked.

19:13.210 --> 19:15.460
There you go, keeping everything bottled up.

19:15.880 --> 19:17.960
We can't understand you if you don't talk to us.

19:18.790 --> 19:20.580
That's enough, you two.

19:20.580 --> 19:23.080
Right now we need to focus on the mission.

19:23.080 --> 19:24.130
You're right.

19:24.130 --> 19:26.000
Hey, you just ate something!

19:26.000 --> 19:27.040
I'm eating nothing.

19:27.040 --> 19:29.130
You put something in your mouth!
I know you did!

19:29.130 --> 19:30.630
We're on the job!
You can at least wait until...

19:44.080 --> 19:45.710
There aren't any passengers.

19:45.710 --> 19:49.580
This train is transporting contraband,
so it makes sense, but...

19:50.080 --> 19:52.710
But we're not seeing any guards, either.

19:54.960 --> 19:56.170
Be careful!

20:05.880 --> 20:07.080
Now then...

20:08.080 --> 20:10.500
Might I see your tickets?

20:12.420 --> 20:15.380
Oh, please! You think this will...

20:16.670 --> 20:19.210
It's kind of unbreakable!

20:19.880 --> 20:21.750
Magically reinforced thread!

20:21.830 --> 20:23.040
Who are you?

20:23.040 --> 20:24.960
John Smith.

20:31.290 --> 20:33.130
You voluntarily put yourself within death's reach

20:33.130 --> 20:35.290
to eliminate the distance between
yourself and your enemy.

20:35.290 --> 20:36.960
That was the correct choice.

20:36.960 --> 20:38.170
However...

20:39.040 --> 20:41.460
You're too inexperienced to risk
it all on a single attack.

20:41.960 --> 20:43.170
Number 666!

20:43.790 --> 20:47.380
I knew you people would be the first to figure it out.

20:47.880 --> 20:49.460
But it's too soon.

20:50.920 --> 20:52.330
You do not need...

20:52.580 --> 20:54.380
...to learn any more.

20:54.750 --> 20:55.960
Not yet!

21:11.420 --> 21:13.000
Stop! I still haven't-

21:13.000 --> 21:14.250
Number 666!

21:15.420 --> 21:17.750
It's over, Number 666.

21:17.750 --> 21:19.000
But...

21:19.000 --> 21:21.630
If we go after him without a plan,
we'll fall into the exact same trap.

21:22.170 --> 21:24.500
Surely you're smart enough to understand that.

21:26.830 --> 21:29.580
Aww, they started speeding up.

21:30.040 --> 21:32.750
I don't think we can catch up now, even if we run.

21:34.830 --> 21:37.130
We go back and report to Lady Gamma.

21:37.130 --> 21:38.330
Understood?

21:39.420 --> 21:40.630
Yes...

21:45.540 --> 21:47.000
John Smith...

21:48.380 --> 21:49.920
That power...

21:52.250 --> 21:53.500
Why?

21:54.210 --> 21:56.960
Why am I so...

21:58.290 --> 21:59.500
Why...

22:00.880 --> 22:02.710
Why am I so weak?

22:24.420 --> 22:28.290
An endlessly deep dark night
Doko made mo fukai yamiyo to<b></b>

22:28.290 --> 22:31.130
I thought, as I closed my eyes
Omotte me o tsubutteta<b></b>

22:31.130 --> 22:36.330
Still unaware of the voice of the star calling out to me
Yobikakeru hoshi no koe ni kizukenai mama<b></b>

22:36.710 --> 22:40.670
A faint light, not too bright
Mabushiku wa nai awai hi<b></b>

22:40.670 --> 22:43.420
But comforting, that's how you were
Kokochi ii sonna anata o<b></b>

22:43.420 --> 22:47.290
Before I knew it, I was following you with my eyes
Shiranu uchi ni me de oikaketa<b></b>

22:47.290 --> 22:49.880
Even if I run out of breath
Iki o kirashite<b></b>

22:50.290 --> 22:53.330
And start to stumble
Motsuresou ni natte mo<b></b>

22:53.330 --> 22:55.580
I've never felt this before
Kono kimochi wa hajimete<b></b>

22:55.580 --> 22:59.500
I can't stop the feeling
Mita koto no nai jibun ni aeru<b></b>

22:59.880 --> 23:03.330
That I can meet a me I've never seen before
Yokan ga tomaranai<b></b>

23:03.830 --> 23:06.750
I run down the path in front of me
Me no mae no michi o hashiru<b></b>

23:06.750 --> 23:09.830
I run far, even when I'm lost
Tooku, mayotte mo<b></b>

23:09.830 --> 23:13.670
If I look up, you won't have changed
Miagereba anata wa kawaranaide<b></b>

23:13.670 --> 23:16.040
You'll be there
Soko ni iru koto o<b></b>

23:16.040 --> 23:19.000
It may be strange, but I can believe it
Fushigi demo shinjirareru<b></b>

23:19.000 --> 23:22.040
Kaze ga tsuyoi hi mo
Even on windy days<b></b>

23:22.040 --> 23:26.540
I don't have to try to reach over you
Over you todokeyou to shinakutatte ii<b></b>

23:26.540 --> 23:28.880
Hey (Did you know?)
Nee (Shitteru?)<b></b>

23:28.880 --> 23:31.920
As all the stars revolve
Subete no hoshi ga mawarinagara<b></b>

23:31.920 --> 23:35.170
I keep my sights on you
Anata o mezashiteru<b></b>

23:35.170 --> 23:38.130
Polaris in the Night
